<title>USA: FSA qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Bullhead City School District No 15, Ariz., $6.355 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Paradise Valley Unified School District No 69, Ariz., $38.565 million school bonds.  </p>
<p>--Shirley, Mass., $1.045 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hainesport Township, N.J., $6.55 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Wyckoff Township Board of Education, N.J., $3.6 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Augusta School District, Wis., $7.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
